For all designs I ask you to make, have them be beautiful, not cookie cutter. Make webpages that are fully featured and worthy for production.

By default, this template supports JSX syntax with Tailwind CSS classes, React hooks, and Lucide React for icons. Do not install other packages for UI themes, icons, etc unless absolutely necessary or I request them.

Use icons from lucide-react for logos.

Import project modules with the `@/` path alias, which maps to `src/` (e.g. `@/components/Foo` == `src/components/Foo`), instead of deep relative paths like `../../components/Foo`.

# Houndly – standing rules

- UK British English in all copy. Dates as 30 Oct 2026, 24-hour times, weight in kg.
- Mobile first from 360 px, responsive to laptop (1280 px). Bottom navigation on phone, sidebar on laptop.
- Stack: React, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Supabase (Auth, Postgres, Storage, Edge Functions). Do not switch frameworks.
- Security: RLS on every table and on the dog-photos bucket. Every row has owner_id = auth.uid(). Never put API keys in front-end code. OPENAI_API_KEY lives only in Supabase secrets and is used only by the generate-checklist Edge Function.
- AI safety: the AI only reformats the owner's own instructions into tasks. It never adds medical advice, tasks, doses, drugs or durations. The Checklist Builder shows: "Houndly is not a vet. It only organises the instructions you paste in. If you're unsure, check with your vet."
- Accessibility: WCAG 2.2 AA. Labelled inputs, 4.5:1 text contrast, 44 px tap targets, flags shown by icon and text, not colour alone.
- Look and feel: warm and friendly. Soft greens and creams, rounded cards, gentle shadows, friendly dog touches; calm, not childish.
- Work on one feature at a time. Do not change files unrelated to the current request.
